From 0021a097b42e889b0c7927c9db465ac6bec1c2ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The wider screen and SPEED: fixes from a playthrough
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SPEED is held at 1x while the start menu and what it opened are up
(PORT_SPEED_HOLD_MENU), released when the player walks again: only the
walking and the field go faster.

A Pokémon caught with the party full may take a party member's place: in
the battle, before the nickname, "Your party is full. Add X to your
party?" (battle_script.c); YES opens the battle's party screen to pick
the one that goes to the PC (any of them: battle_party.c; its SHIFT reads
SEND TO PC, battle_party_text.c), then "X was added to the party and Y
was sent to the PC." (not one with Mail or a Ball Capsule, which the PC
doesn't take). The caught one goes to the PC as ever, the battle noting
where; the two change places once the battle's party is back in the save
(encounter.c, UpdateFieldSystemFromDTO). Not in the Safari Zone, Pal
Park or the catching tutorial.

Selling in a Poké Mart with the lower screen's menu keeps the store on
the upper screen (shop_menu.c: its message layer cleared, then held).

A new game saves over the old save, as if that had been erased first
(SaveData_OverwriteCheck: never a different game's save to refuse; the
main menu's NEW GAME warning about it skipped; SaveDataExtra_Init starts
the Hall of Fame anew with the rest of the extra data).

On the remaster's wider upper screen:
- the screen indicator at a text box's top right is told to the port
  (NitroPort_WindowIndicator: set by Text_RenderScreenIndicator, cleared
  when the window or that corner is cleared or the text scrolls), which
  draws it at the widened box's right edge; a BG set up anew or freed is
  told too (NitroPort_WideBgReset: the text box frames kept there go);
- the Pokédex's registration page: the Pokémon's box 24 pixels to the
  left with its 3D Pokémon, the title 24 to the right; its left edge the
  page's border carried on (not the footprint's arc again); the entry's
  text wrapped again across the wider box (InfoMain_PortRewrap; a word
  split at its hyphen joined again);
- the evolution's background: its edge columns carried on beside the
  DS's screen (its map's other half came round there);
- the battle's trainers slide off past the wider screen's edges (the
  battle's OAM culled at the wider screen's edges: NitroPort_WideCells);
- the HM cut-in: the band of Poké Balls repeats to the screen's edges;
  the Pokémon waits beyond the wider screen's right edge and slides off
  past its left one;
- the scripts' people: one added beside the DS's picture but not beyond
  the wider one's is put beyond it and walks the extra tiles in with its
  first steps; one whose walk out ends there walks the extra tiles out;
  one walking straight out through something the DS's picture didn't
  show goes round it (the ground's collisions, ledges and cliffs, the
  height carried along the way; the other people standing there too,
  not the ones the script sets walking with it).
  One whose first commands turn it or wait is moved before it's drawn.
  When the script ends, or the next one starts (script_manager.c), the
  ones still moved go back where the script put them;
- Route 201's Pokémon Breeder stands 5 tiles further right
  (map_header_data.c, sPortWideMoves): Rowan and Dawn walked through him.
